{"data": {"acceptance": ["A whitespace-only edit that merges a paragraph pair before a scene separator and splits a paragraph after it, preserving the total count, leaves the explicit marker as scene_separator and assigns no prose paragraph scene_separator.", "A subsequent deterministic chunking run omits only the explicit scene marker and materializes every prose fragment from the edited Cleanup text.", "Whitespace-only edits with unambiguously matching paragraph content preserve existing noncontradicted roles, including headings, regardless of index shifts.", "Unmatched or ambiguously repeated paragraph content falls back to classifier-only roles rather than raw-index roles.", "Existing aligned-edit role preservation, explicit scene-separator classification, Cleanup downstream invalidation, and valid Chunking behavior remain green under focused regression coverage.", "Focused Cleanup and deterministic Chunking tests, focused Ruff/compile checks, and traceability/coverage audits pass; the full pytest suite is not run by explicit human instruction and manual application testing remains required before publishing."], "assumptions": ["Use the ticket's better fix: carry prior noncontradicted roles only for unambiguous normalized-content matches; unmatched or ambiguous records retain classifier-only roles.", "A stale prior scene_separator role is never carried onto text that the current conservative classifier does not recognize as a scene separator."], "created_at": "2026-07-30T05:58:14+00:00", "decision": "proceed", "open_questions": [], "planned_paths": ["04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/services/text_cleanup_service.py", "04_Software/AudioMancer/tests/test_cleanup_v2_service.py", "04_Software/AudioMancer/tests/test_cleanup_v2_quality_contract.py", ".agentic/requirements/functional/REQ-FUNC-807c56f0-12b7-42e9-bd8f-0d562c903e70.toml", ".agentic/specs/cleanup_chunking_v2.spec.md", ".agentic/knowledge/components/Text_Cleanup.md"], "reason": "The failure and downstream consequence are reproduced by a narrow persisted-role branch, the content-match policy is deterministic and conservative, existing requirements already bound the contract, and focused end-to-end coverage can prove no prose is lost without changing Chunking semantics.", "recommended_responses": [], "risk": "low", "scope": ["In scope: whitespace-only role realignment in save_user_cleaned_text; normalized-content matching for unambiguous prior roles; focused Cleanup-to-deterministic-Chunking regression coverage; the existing whitespace-realignment requirement and Cleanup V2 specification; Text Cleanup documentation review. Out of scope: lexical-edit behavior, scene-separator classifier rules, deterministic or AI Chunking implementation, starts_after_scene_separator issue #35, general paragraph diffing, UI changes, and the full pytest suite explicitly deferred by the human due runtime."], "source": "Gitea issue #32 supplied verbatim by the human; remediation order in master issue #40; automated continuation and focused-validation override supplied 2026-07-30", "understanding": "Whitespace-only manual Cleanup edits currently preserve roles by list index whenever the paragraph count is unchanged. A merge before an existing scene separator plus a split after it shifts content while preserving count, allowing the old scene_separator role to land on prose. Both deterministic and AI Chunking treat that explicit role as authoritative and omit the prose without warning. Replace index alignment with unambiguous normalized-content matching, preserve classifier-positive scene separators, and fall back to classifier-only roles when content cannot be matched safely."}, "event": "alignment.recorded", "time": "2026-07-30T05:58:14+00:00"}
